# Deploy rules

Read before editing deployment-related files:

- `docs/deploy/README.md`
- `docs/deploy/ARCHITECTURE.md`
- `docs/deploy/OPTIONS.md`
- `docs/deploy/ENVIRONMENT_STRATEGY.md`
- `docs/deploy/CHECKLIST.md`

## Runtime baseline (mandatory)

- All production options run on Docker.
- Traefik is the edge proxy for both options.
- Api and Worker are separate services with separate lifecycle.
- Worker must remain private-only (no public route).

## Routing baseline

- Prefer same-origin browser calls with `/api` path routing to Api.
- Avoid introducing cross-origin API calls unless project requirements explicitly demand a separate public API domain.

## Environment management

- Split env files by environment (`development`, `staging`, `production`) and optionally `shared`.
- Commit only `.env.example` templates; never commit real secrets.
- Keep env key naming consistent and avoid hidden override chains.

## Deployment safety

- Run DB migration before rolling out new Api/Worker versions.
- Keep rollback references (previous image tags) documented.
- Use health checks (`/health/live`, `/health/ready`) as release gates.

## CI/CD expectations

- Option 1 (automated): CI tests/build -> image publish -> migration -> rollout.
- Option 2 (manual): operator-run scripted flow with the same migration/health gates.
- Do not bypass tests and migration checks for convenience.

## Repo layout (when adding deploy code)

- Dockerfiles under `deploy/docker/<service>/` with build `context: ../..` (repo root).
- Application source stays in `src/` — do not duplicate app code under `deploy/`.
- Compose files: `deploy/compose/stack.yml`, `deploy/compose/traefik.yml`.
- Infra compose: `deploy/compose/infra.yml` (shared services).
- Use `deploy/scripts/*.sh` for migrate/up/build entrypoints.
- Commit only `*.env.example`; real `*.env` stays gitignored under `deploy/env/`.
